# Files that run inside the Linux container keep LF whatever the checkout does.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF has "#!/bin/sh\r" as its shebang, and the
# kernel looks for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r". The error is "no such file
# or directory" naming a file that plainly exists, which is a bad hour for
# whoever hits it. This repository is developed on Windows, so it would happen.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
docker-compose.yaml text eol=lf
docker-compose.scale.yaml text eol=lf
docker-compose.observability*.yaml text eol=lf
docker-compose.dev.yaml text eol=lf
deploy/observability/* text eol=lf

# Documents are bytes. A small PDF holds no NUL byte, so git guessed "text" and a
# Windows checkout rewrote its line endings: the file then failed to convert, and
# the scorecard with it, on any fresh clone.
*.pdf           binary
*.docx          binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.pptx          binary
*.zip           binary
*.png           binary
